              "text": "As of mid-2026, the latest iPhone lineup consists of the **iPhone 17 series** (including the standard **iPhone 17**, the thin **iPhone Air**, the **iPhone 17 Pro**, and **iPhone 17 Pro Max**) alongside the budget-friendly **iPhone 17e**. \n\nYou can purchase these models from several official and authorized channels, depending on whether you want to buy the phone outright (unlocked) or on a carrier contract:\n\n### 1. Directly from Apple (Best for Unlocked Phones & Direct Trade-Ins)\nBuying straight from Apple is the most straightforward way to get a fully unlocked phone with no carrier strings attached.\n*   **Apple Store Online & Apple Store App:** You can configure your model, storage size (note that the standard iPhone 17 base model now starts at 256GB instead of 128GB), and color.\n*   **Physical Apple Stores:** If you want to check out the colors in person, you can visit a local retail location. \n*   **Benefits:** You can use **Apple Trade In** to get credit (often several hundred dollars) toward your new phone by trading in an older model. You can also easily add AppleCare+ or opt for Apple Card Monthly Installments.\n\n### 2. Mobile/Wireless Carriers (Best for Promotional Deals & Bill Credits)\nIf you don't mind staying with your carrier for 24 to 36 months, major networks offer massive trade-in promotions that can make the latest iPhone significantly cheaper (or sometimes even \"free\" via bill credits).\n*   **In the US:** AT&T, T-Mobile, and Verizon all offer heavy promotions on the iPhone 17 and 17 Pro series, especially when trading in a relatively recent device (like an iPhone 13 or newer) and signing up for an eligible unlimited plan.\n*   **In the UK & Europe:** Major carriers like EE, Vodafone, O2, and Three offer monthly contract plans that bundle the phone with a data package.\n*   **Benefits:** Low upfront cost and the ability to finance the device over a multi-year contract.\n\n### 3. Major Authorized Retailers (Best for Store Rewards & Financing)\nMany major retail chains are authorized Apple sellers. They frequently run their own financing deals or offer store rewards.\n*   **Best Buy:** Frequently matches carrier promotions and offers its own financing options. It is also a great place to pick up the phone the same day.\n*   **Target & Walmart:** Excellent options for buying both carrier-locked and select unlocked models, occasionally bundled with retail gift cards during sales events.\n*   **Amazon:** Make sure you are purchasing directly from the **Official Apple Store on Amazon** to guarantee you are getting a genuine, brand-new device with a full warranty. \n\n### Quick Tips Before You Buy:\n*   **Check the storage:** If you are buying the base iPhone 17, keep in mind that the minimum storage size is 256GB, so you might not need to pay extra to upgrade your storage unless you take a massive amount of 4K video. \n*   **Carrier-locked vs. Unlocked:** If you travel internationally, buy an *unlocked* phone from Apple or an authorized retailer so you can easily swap in local eSIMs.",
